# Git Cleanup and Push to Remote Repository
## Check Repository Status
```bash
git status
```
---
## View Available Branches
```bash
git branch
```
To view both local and remote branches:
```bash
git branch -a
```
---
## Switch to Master Branch
```bash
git checkout master
```
If your repository uses `main`:
```bash
git checkout main
```
---
## Pull Latest Changes
For master:
```bash
git pull origin master
```
For main:
```bash
git pull origin main
```
---
## Push Local Changes
For master:
```bash
git push origin master
```
For main:
```bash
git push origin main
```
---
## Verify Changes
Open the GitHub repository and refresh the page to verify that the latest commits are available.
---
## Commands Used
```bash
git status
git branch
git branch -a
git checkout master
git pull origin master
git push origin master
```
## Result
- Verified the repository was in a clean state.
- Listed all available branches.
- Pulled the latest changes from the remote repository.
- Pushed local commits to the remote repository.
- Verified that the changes were updated successfully on GitHub.
